      "side": 0,
      "message": "There is build error caused by config after I remove EC_BRINGUP.\n\nWhen this config is enabled, it selects PLATFORM_EC_BYPASS_CBI_EEPROM_WP_CHECK by default, then legacy EC flag CONFIG_BYPASS_CBI_EEPROM_WP_CHECK is enabled as a result, which requires either CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED, or CONFIG_EEPROM_CBI_WP to be enabled in include/config.h.\n\nSo to keep CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_EEPROM_CBI_WP, need to set CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED, or CONFIG_EEPROM_CBI_WP. But CONFIG_EEPROM_CBI_WP is not available to zephyr code. And \nCONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED should not be enabled even in development phase I think. (EC_BRINGUP select CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED, that\u0027s why the build is ok)\n\nIf need to keep this flag, the only choice is to add CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED\u003dy, not sure if this could be a long term plan.",
